      "id": "minimax-h3-heptagram-v2-t2v",
      "name": "MiniMax H3 Text to Video (Heptagram v2)",
      "icon": "🎬",
      "previewImage": "previews/minimax-h3-heptagram-v2-t2v.jpg",
      "description": "Text to video on eatyet's Heptagram v2 Entropy preview, a merged checkpoint with the TaoMate and HyperFlow speed LoRAs built in, so there is no second file. A five-second shot takes about 80 seconds at 480p and about 3 1/2 minutes at 768p on a 12 GB card.\n\nThis is a preview. The author says v2's final form depends on community feedback, so a final release may look different.\n\nIt has a strong look: high contrast, dense surface detail and big expressions. Pick it for punch, and pick another card for soft or natural pictures. On a 3D cartoon test, flour came out as thick clumps on the cook's face.\n\nIt does not hold a still shot. On a locked-off prompt, movement in the frame measured about three times stock H3's on all three seeds, and the camera pushed in on the clip we checked in the app.\n\nSound runs very loud. Busy prompts sat about 16 dB above stock H3. A prompt for quiet room tone and faint distant traffic came out about 30 dB above stock, with no recognisable words but a constant low rumble that sits louder than the character's breath. If you want near silence, pick another card.\n\nThe Steps control covers the author's 4 to 8. Only 8 was tested here, and the author says 8 clearly improves picture and sound.\n\nThis is a separate download from Heptagram Turbo.\n\nMiniMax H3 Community License. Read its territorial and commercial-use terms before commercial use.\n\nModel format: int8 ConvRot.",
